{
  "_comment": [
    "Shows the sitemap lists whether or not anyone has followed one.",
    "",
    "Every id was resolved against TMDb and checked, not typed from memory: a title search returns",
    "the wrong country more often than not for a format that has been remade everywhere. MasterChef",
    "first resolved to the Polish version, Kingdom to a Japanese anime rather than the Korean drama,",
    "Heart Signal and Perfect Match and The Ultimatum to editions nobody here meant. Each entry was",
    "re-checked against the origin country its category implies, which is what caught those five.",
    "",
    "Chosen for genre spread over personal taste - reality, Korean reality, K-drama and soaps are the",
    "audiences this app is for, and they are the shows with the large, shifting casts that are hard",
    "to keep straight, which is the problem it solves.",
    "",
    "'name' is TMDb's own, kept so a future reader can tell at a glance whether an id still points at",
    "what it says. Nothing reads it at runtime; the sitemap needs only the ids.",
    "",
    "Editing: add a line, resolve the id against TMDb first, and keep them unique. The sitemap unions",
    "this with whatever is in shows:watched, so a duplicate here is harmless but a wrong id is a URL",
    "that renders someone else's show."
  ],
